      "leftForReview": {
        "issues": [
          "node/global-require L38",
          "unicorn/prefer-module L38"
        ],
        "explanation": "I left both issues unchanged. The `require()` on line 38 is a conditional load, so neither of the usual fixes keeps the code working the same way:\n\n- **Moving it to a top-level static `import`** (what both rules suggest) would load `../shared/lib/i18n/normalize-locale-path` every time. The branch exists so the i18n module is only pulled in when `process.env.__NEXT_I18N_SUPPORT` is set. With the guard in place, Next.js's build can drop that module from the client bundle when i18n is off. A static import would always include it, which the task rules also say not to do.\n- **Switching to `import()`** would make the loading asynchronous. `normalizeLocalePath` would then return a Promise instead of `{ pathname, detectedLocale }`, which breaks its `typeof Fn` signature and every caller that expects a result straight away.\n\nThe only way to clear these issues is to change how the module is loaded, such as having the bundler swap in a stub when i18n is off. That's a build-configuration change outside this file, not a lint fix. The lazy `require` may simply be meant to stay, in which case these two rules shouldn't apply to this file."
      },
      "leftForReviewShare": "all",
      "leftForReviewRules": [
        "node/global-require",
        "unicorn/prefer-module"
      ],
